faqs:
- q: Can you help me move a parent with dementia?
  a: 'Yes. We help with the practical side: sorting with the family, careful packing, a fully insured removal and setting up the new home, with one coordinator. We do not give medical or care advice, so ask your parent&rsquo;s GP or care team about their needs.'
- q: How do you keep the move calm?
  a: We plan the day with you around your parent&rsquo;s routine where we can, use our own vetted team, and put familiar things such as photographs, bedding and a favourite chair in place early. Our guide to <a href="/blog/moving-house-with-dementia-in-the-family/">moving house with dementia</a> has more practical ideas.
- q: Can my parent stay somewhere else on moving day?
  a: That is for you and your parent&rsquo;s care team to decide. Many families arrange for a relative or friend to spend the day with them away from the packing, and we plan the day with that in mind.
- q: Who decides whether my parent should move?
  a: The decision belongs to your parent and their family, with their GP, care team and, where legal authority is needed, their solicitor. See our guide to <a href="/blog/lasting-power-of-attorney-moving-a-parent/">power of attorney and moving a parent</a>. We do not give legal or medical advice.
- q: Can you help move a parent into a care home?
  a: Yes. See our <a href="/care-home-removals/">care home removals</a> page, which covers choosing what fits in a smaller room, packing, the removal and setting the room up.
- q: How much does it cost?
  a: Chayce packages start at {bronze} for packing and an insured removal. Silver Comfort at {silver} adds sorting and declutter help, a deep clean and unpacking with a coordinator. A Discovery Consultation costs {discovery}. The final price depends on the size of the home and is confirmed in writing before you book.
- q: I live far away. Can I still arrange the move?
  a: Yes. Moves are often arranged by adult children on a parent&rsquo;s behalf. You can be involved by phone or video, and your coordinator keeps you updated throughout.
- q: Is the removal insured?
  a: Yes. Every Chayce removal is fully insured against loss or damage in transit, and the cover is set out in your service agreement before the move begins.
- q: Do you work outside Northampton?
  a: Yes. We are based in Northampton and arrange moves across the whole UK.
